! Consume Archive — where the early research landed

''This is the only record of which scratch note became which doctrine.'' The research files are gone;
what they contributed stands in the memes below, and this table is the rope between them.

Read it as provenance, never as a worklist. The pass it records closed, and the sources it names were
deleted on 2026-05-16 — so a row here answers "where did this come from", and nothing here is owed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/history>>

!! Origin-story records

''These three were named by an index and never carried.'' They preserved development-arc material — the
conversations and early drafts behind current doctrine — and the 2026-05-16 pass deleted their sources
before any carrier held them. The rows stand as a record of what the corpus does NOT hold.

The arc that DID survive stands at [[lindwyrm|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/lindwyrm/index]], and
[[period-forms|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/period-forms]] governs how its early HUD reads.

| Named, not held | Would have preserved |
|---|---|
| `genesis-sharktooth-chatlog` | April 12 2026 Gemini chatlog; shark-teeth origin; Shape/Detail/Motion genesis; Wild Magic first taxonomy |
| `prior-art-comparison` | 8-system prior-art comparison; per-system design pressure; 7 v5 spec design tests |
| `mu-emergence-sequence` | Boot grammar emergence narrative; four-layer model origin; null-oracle first statement |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/index>>

